// Issue #634: edit data in the layer control that a calculation rule configures.
//
// Run with MicroTst.dms. /Issue634/hoek_calc is themed on /Issue634/calc_classes, whose
// classBreaks, BrushColor and Label are all genuinely calculated, so each edit below has to copy
// its attribute before it can write. hoek_classes/PenColor cannot serve for this: it is a plain
// reference and resolves through to the editable data block hoek_classes/BrushColor.
//
// Expected in the log:
//   - an "Execute" line per menu item named below,
//   - one "Edit: /Issue634/calc_classes/<attr> is configured or calculated ... was created for
//     this desktop and is edited instead (issue #634)" per attribute, and never twice for the
//     same one, naming a copy under /Desktops/Default/ViewData/Issue634/calc_classes/,
//   - no errors.
//
// Sub-object indices are 1-based; a 0 ends the path. In the palette editor,
//   {6,1,1,N} is the header caption of column N,
//   {6,2,1,N} is column N itself, which is what keyboard input needs:
//   1 = BrushColor, 2 = Label, 3 = classBreaks, 4 = area, 5 = count.
// Menu items are addressed by the left part of their caption rather than by position. That
// matters most here: the two routes above give menus that differ by the Ramp Colors entry, so
// every index would differ between them. A name that matches nothing, or that matches more than
// one item, is reported as an error.

ActivateItem "/Issue634/hoek_calc"
DefaultView
WAIT 8000

// LayerControl popup, same item as in MapViewClassification.dmsscript
SEND 4 2 1 "Edit Palette"
WAIT 4000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the colour
// Change Color -> Set to transparent: a colour edit that needs no modal colour dialogue.
SEND 4 5 0 6 2 1 1
WAIT 1000
SEND 4 3 1 "Change Color" "Set to transparent"
WAIT 3000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the label
// TextEditController starts an in-cell edit on the first WM_CHAR when it is not already editing.
SEND 4 5 0 6 2 1 2
WAIT 1000
SEND 3 3 258 88 0  // 258=WM_CHAR, 88='X'
WAIT 800
SEND 3 3 256 13 0  // 256=WM_KEYDOWN, 13=VK_RETURN: commit
WAIT 3000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the class break
SEND 4 5 0 6 2 1 3
WAIT 1000
SEND 3 3 258 50 0  // WM_CHAR, 50='2'
WAIT 800
SEND 3 3 256 13 0  // VK_RETURN
WAIT 3000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the copy is reused
// The same colour edit again must NOT report a second copy: the first one is edited further.
SEND 4 5 0 6 2 1 1
WAIT 1000
SEND 4 3 1 "Change Color" "Set to transparent"
WAIT 3000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- inspect the result
// Copy Classbreaks (#734) puts the edited breaks, colours and labels on the clipboard, so a
// run can be inspected by hand: class 0 must read 2;rgb(0,0,0);"X" against the configured
// 0;rgb(0,0,255);"calc class 0".
SEND 4 2 1 "Copy Classbreaks"
WAIT 1500

SEND 1 3 16 0 0
